Description:
Datura is een onderzoeksbureau en laboratorium dat innovatieve meettechnieken onderzoekt en ontwikkelt voor toepassingen in de praktijk en specialistische vakkennis heeft op het gebied van eDNA-toepassingen. Met onze technieken maken we ecologische monitoring effectiever en efficiënter en dragen we bij aan de bescherming en de kwaliteit van onze natuur en leefomgeving.

Onze diensten (o.a.): 
- Monitoring van biodiversiteit door middel van eDNA. Datura heeft primers ontwikkeld waarmee eDNA van specifieke soorten (qPCR) of soortgroepen (metabarcoding) gedetecteerd kan worden;
- Monitoring van biologische, chemische en fysische aspecten van bodem- waterkwaliteit;
- Identificatie van soorten op basis van DNA, dieetanalyses, populatiegenetica en meer.

The COZYME(COmputationally assisted design of enZYMEs) Action comprises a Pan-European collaborative network to develop and implement state-of-the-art computational tools for rapid enzyme improvement.

To meet the growing demand for tailored enzymes for novel industrial applications, a rapid and efficient workflow for protein redesign and optimization is urgently needed, together with researchers trained in computational enzyme redesign. This is required to overcome the “number crunching”, time-consuming and expensive problems typically associated with protein engineering. For this challenge, transnational collaboration is essential, bringing together different fields of expertise. To this end, the COZYME network will develop innovative computational tools for enzyme engineering and constructing and evaluating enzyme variants. 

The main activities of COZYME Action focus on:

• Sharing of knowledge, software code, experimental data, skills, materials and infrastructure;
• Exchange and training of PhD students and early career investigators;
• Integration of public and private sectors;
• Establishing a platform for career development and collaboration;
• Implementation of an effective communication strategy that involves EU institutions and policymakers;
• Increasing the impact of the Action by execution of joint exploitation and dissemination plans;
• Organization of workshops, training schools and webinars on computational enzyme engineering open to the scientific community and interested stakeholders.

We develop methods that will allow:
*to preserve whole human brains in a way that conserves the ultrastructure of cells and their connections, essentially forever;
*to analyze the 3-dimensional structure and molecular composition of the cells in human brains with nanometer resolution;  
*to understand how these cells connect, store, and process information. 

Our research spans neuroscience, computer science, philosophy (bioethics), and social science. In our social science research, we query relevant stakeholders (including neuroscientists and medical doctors). We would like to identify the barriers to research on how the human brain works and how disease (mostly neurological disease, often associated with aging) affects the structure of the brain. 

We collaborate with public and private scientific institutions in Europe and the United States and welcome new collaborations and ideas on how to attract more interest in and funding for our work.

LifeSciences@Work (LS@W) is an accelerator program for Life Sciences start-ups and entrepreneurial scientist that want to turn their breakthrough invention into a business. LS@W includes the Venture Challenge, Expert Classes, Value Centre and Alumni, Mentor and Expert Community.
LS@W is powered by Health~Holland. 

Working with us means: you start a successful company that will make a difference.

We help researchers
- to transform breakthrough research and groundbreaking inventions into clear startup business cases;
- to strengthen their existing business case;
- to prepare their startup for market fit and growth;
- to obtain funding, partners and market introductions;
and to introduce aspiring life sciences entrepreneurs to valuable communities including venture capitalists, industry experts, seasoned entrepreneurs, LS@W alumni.

Only the best ideas based on excellent science, with high growth potential, large commercial and societal benefits, and an international scope will be selected by LS@W. After admittance, you can profit by participating in the Venture Challenge, Expert Classes and Value Centre. These three stages of the accelerator programme are developed to help scientists build their own business.

